course: dictionary
lesson: 4364
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word guru can mean a holy teacher, or it can mean an expert. «Ask Mia, she's our maths guru» is not about religion, so here guru means someone who knows a lot and can help you.
explain: Religion words often come with names or places. «Sikhism was founded by Guru Nanak in the Punjab about 500 years ago» tells you that a Guru is a holy teacher and guide, because the sentence talks about a faith and the person who started it.
explain: Ask yourself: what kind of text is this? A story about a faith needs the religious meaning. A chatty sentence about who knows the most about phones needs the everyday meaning. Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: In Hinduism and Sikhism, a guru is a holy teacher and guide.
fact: Sikhs honour ten human Gurus, and Guru Nanak founded Sikhism about 500 years ago in the Punjab.
fact: Sikhs treat their holy book, the Guru Granth Sahib, with honour as a living Guru.
fact: In everyday talk, a guru is an expert that others go to for advice, like «a computer guru» or «a fitness guru».
fact: «Guru» came from Sanskrit, the ancient language of India, and it means teacher.
exercise: «Ask Mia, she's our maths guru.» In this sentence, what is a guru? | A holy teacher in a gurdwara | *An expert who knows a lot and gives advice | A holy book | A type of temple
exercise: «Sikhism was founded by Guru Nanak in the Punjab.» Which meaning of guru fits here? | A fitness trainer | A computer expert | A sports coach | *A holy teacher and guide
exercise: Which word came from Sanskrit, the ancient language of India, and means teacher? | pundit | *guru | gurdwara | avatar
test: «Online gurus sometimes sell advice that is not true, so check the facts.» What does guru mean in this sentence? | *Someone who gives advice, so we should check what they say | It means a holy book | It means a type of game | It means a gurdwara
test: Which Guru founded Sikhism about 500 years ago in the Punjab? | Guru Granth Sahib | The Punjab | Avatar | *Guru Nanak
exam: Jayden reads «She is our style guru» and asks what guru means. What is the best answer? | A type of game character | A place where Sikhs pray | *An expert whose advice people trust about style | A holy teacher who leads prayers
